From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:56:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: keep the version of a thread's per monitor DPI
 awareness in its windows.

A top-level window of a thread aware of each monitor's DPI got the
first version of that awareness whichever the thread had, 0x12 where
Windows gives 0x22 for a thread of the second.  The window procedure
runs in the window's awareness, so a per monitor v2 window was told it
was v1 even in its own WM_NCCREATE.  The version now comes from the
thread; the DPI and the flags are still dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c8a9043e99f5fb33873e2e3c906f4665bf6e42a2)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index a0dd77d3a71..d436ceb877f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5884,11 +5884,11 @@ static WND *create_window_handle( HWND parent, HWND owner, UNICODE_STRING *name,
     struct tagCLASS *class = NULL;
     WND *win;
 
-    if (NTUSER_DPI_CONTEXT_IS_MONITOR_AWARE( dpi_context ) && dpi_context != NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE)
-    {
-        FIXME( "DPI context %#x not implemented\n", dpi_context );
-        dpi_context = NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE;
-    }
+    /* As on Windows, a window of a thread aware of each monitor's DPI is aware of it in the version the thread
+     * is, 0x22 for the second, and of no DPI in particular. */
+    if (NTUSER_DPI_CONTEXT_IS_MONITOR_AWARE( dpi_context ))
+        dpi_context = MAKE_NTUSER_DPI_CONTEXT( DPI_AWARENESS_PER_MONITOR_AWARE,
+                                               NTUSER_DPI_CONTEXT_GET_VERSION( dpi_context ), 0, 0 );
 
     if (!is_desktop_class( name ))
     {
